    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (70.72) and **Kyle Tucker** (66.88), our two highest-projected assets. **Gunnar Henderson** holds the edge today due to a favorable interaction with the opposing pitcher's delivery; facing Gausman, his elite speed is bolstered by a \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus, heightening his potential in our scarcest category, SB. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (64.21) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (63.63) present high-floor starts, with both benefiting significantly from dynamic platoon advantages against Brazob\u00e1n and Soroka, respectively. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.55) remains a locked-in core play, as his raw power profile overrides the marginal skill of Baz, keeping him firmly in the Strong category.\n\nThe most difficult decision was the final UTIL slot, where **Miguel Vargas** (48.58) narrowly edged out **Nolan Schanuel** (41.09). While **Nolan Schanuel** showed a solid base projection, his score was suppressed by a difficult matchup against Sheehan, resulting in a suboptimal SP Skill adjustment. **Miguel Vargas** earns the nod primarily due to his batting order stability; despite facing a capable arm in Nola, his positioning in the two-hole provides the volume required to outpace **Nolan Schanuel**\u2019s ceiling today. Note that **Miguel Andujar** remains a high-risk play (41.69), hovering just above our \"Below Floor\" threshold; we are prioritizing his roster spot to preserve daily game caps while monitoring his dynamic platoon variance closely.\n\nManagers should remain alert to the situational risks surrounding our catching and speed-focused assets. Both **Jackson Merrill** and **Miguel Vargas** see slight efficiency deductions due to the opposing backstops' pop times, which may mitigate our aggressiveness on the basepaths. Additionally, while **Liam Hicks** (44.71) is starting, his output is currently hampered by an elite-arm penalty against Jax; he is a marginal play required to maintain depth. We are continuing to track the availability of **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined, but we are positioned to pivot should any late-inning weather alerts surface at these venues.",
